      <description align="center" color="purple" colored="true" height="631" resized="true" width="290" x="353" y="14">FE intialization</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="104" resized="false" width="180" x="388" y="364">FE Intialization&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: Mapping tags&lt;br&gt;I/P 2: Tag data&lt;br&gt;I/P 3: Model alert&lt;br&gt;I/P 4: ccp_info</description>
      <description align="center" color="yellow" colored="false" height="629" resized="true" width="234" x="648" y="16">Main</description>
      <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="229" resized="false" width="180" x="666" y="307">The Tag Imputation Block handles faulty data issues in tags. Users can configure it via the Case Configuration Portal (CCP) to apply default values, use the last known good value, or leave data unchanged based on selected settings&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;O/P 1: Tag data&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: model alert&lt;br&gt;</description>
      <description align="center" color="green" colored="true" height="634" resized="true" width="344" x="10" y="10">data imputation&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Auther:&lt;br&gt;1. Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;2. Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;3. Karthik sangapalli&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Overview:&lt;br&gt;This block manages faulty PI tag data using configurable options in the Case Configuration Portal (CCP). Users can choose actions like applying default values, using last known values, or skipping adjustments, enabling smooth analysis based on selected logic.&lt;br&gt;Input:&lt;br&gt;1: Mapping tags&lt;br&gt;2: Tag data&lt;br&gt;3: Model alert&lt;br&gt;4: ccp_info&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Input macros:&lt;br&gt;1. endtime&lt;br&gt;2. model_id&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Output:&lt;br&gt;1. tag_data&lt;br&gt;2. model_alert&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
    </process>
  </operator>
</process>
